.\" Man page for the packaged dsh launcher.
.TH DSH 1 "September 2026" "deepseek-harness 0.1.5~rc1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dsh \- boot a DeepSeek Harness profile (agent CLI and browser UI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dsh
.RI [ launcher-options ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ app-arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dsh
boots a DeepSeek Harness
.IR profile :
an ordered stack of plugin-bundle patch layers with your own overrides applied
on top. The invoking directory becomes the workspace root.
.PP
This package installs the upstream self-contained runtime, so no system Node.js
is required. The launcher defaults
.B DSH_HOME
to
.I ~/.dsh
and applies the packaged overlay
.I /usr/libexec/dsh/patches/00-packaged-workarounds.yml
when a profile is booted (see PACKAGING below).
.PP
The launcher parses only its own options. The first token it does not recognize
starts the booted profile's own arguments, so app flags belong after the profile
selection:
.PP
.EX
dsh web --port 8080
dsh --profile headless "run the tests"
.EE
.SH LAUNCHER OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " name"
Boot the profile stored under
.IR $DSH_HOME/profiles/ name .
.TP
.BI \-\-from\-default\-profile " template"
Create a new profile from a shipped template, then boot it.
.TP
.BI \-\-patch " path"
Apply an extra patch-list overlay after the profile layer. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-config
Print the composed profile tree and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-default\-config
Print the profile tree without the user layer or overlays, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the runtime version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B web
Boot the web profile (equivalent to
.BR "\-\-profile web" )
and open the browser UI. This is what the desktop entry runs.
.TP
.BI plugin " pnpm-arguments"
Manage a profile's plugin dependencies by forwarding the remaining arguments to
.B pnpm
in the profile directory. Requires
.B pnpm
to be installed.
.SH WEB PROFILE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
Listen port; 0 lets the OS pick a free one.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " host"
Bind host.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Do not open the browser.
.TP
.BI \-\-trusted\-host " authority"
Extra authority the browser-trust fence accepts. Repeatable.
.PP
The web UI is protected by a browser-trust fence: a bare visit to the listening
port returns 401, and the tokenized URL printed by
.B dsh web
must be used. Plain
.B dsh web
opens that URL for you.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DSH_HOME
State directory (profiles, sessions, settings, credentials).
Defaults to
.IR $HOME/.dsh .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
On first boot the runtime materializes its native addons under
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/pkg
(default
.IR ~/.cache/pkg ).
This directory must be writable.
.TP
.B DSH_LIBEXEC
Directory holding the packaged runtime (default
.IR /usr/libexec/dsh ).
.TP
.B DSH_PACKAGED_PATCH
Set to
.B 0
to skip the packaged overlay, or to a path to substitute another overlay.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/dsh/dsh-runtime
The self-contained runtime executable.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/dsh/dsh-runtime-rg
The ripgrep sidecar, resolved by the runtime as
.IR dsh-runtime-rg .
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/dsh/patches/00-packaged-workarounds.yml
Packaged overlay applied to every profile boot.
.SH PACKAGING
Upstream 0.1.5rc1 omits the peer package
.I @deepseek-ai/dsh-session-title-llm
from its runtime closure, so every shipped profile fails to boot with
ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND. The packaged overlay disables the single row that imports
it, falling back to non-LLM session titles. See
.I /usr/share/doc/deepseek-harness/
and the packaging notes for details and for how to retire the workaround.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the browser UI on a fixed port
.B dsh web --port 8080
.TP
Answer one task and exit
.B dsh --profile headless "summarize this repository"
.TP
Inspect the composed configuration
.B dsh --profile web --dump-config
.SH SEE ALSO
Full upstream documentation:
.UR https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
.UE
